				"text": "The Library is a static totality whose membership is not determined by any particular observer's resolution. Every configuration considered here is already a member of \\(\\mathcal{M}\\). The question is therefore not whether an observer causes a configuration to exist, but whether the observer can maintain a distinction between configurations at its available resolution. Once the observer-specific threshold \\(I_N(O)\\) is introduced, distinguishability becomes relational: the same pair of configurations may be operationally distinguishable to one observer while falling below the resolution threshold of another. This difference belongs to the observer-relative relation, not to the ontological membership of the configurations."
