			  {
				"type": "definition",
				"title": "XOR-Derived Distinction",
				"text": "Let \\(x,y\\in\\mathcal{M}\\). Define the XOR-derived distinction relation as the minimum number of XOR operations required to relate \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) through configurations contained in \\(\\mathcal{M}\\).",
				"latex": "d_{\\oplus}(x,y)=\\min\\left\\{n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0\\mid\\exists z_0,\\ldots,z_n\\in\\mathcal{M},\\ z_0=x,\\ z_n=y,\\ \\forall i<n,\\ \\exists w_i\\in\\mathcal{M}:z_{i+1}=z_i\\oplus w_i\\right\\}",
