				"type": "prose",
				"text": "Because the threshold is indexed by \\(O\\), resolution is explicitly relational rather than universal. It is permitted that \\(I_N(O_1)\\neq I_N(O_2)\\), and consequently that the same pair \\((x,y)\\) is distinguishable to \\(O_1\\) while being indistinguishable to \\(O_2\\). Nothing about this difference requires the configurations themselves to have changed. Only the observer-relative resolution relation has changed."
