				"text": "Two distinct relations must therefore remain separate. Library membership is a structural fact within the formal model: \\(x\\in\\mathcal{M}\\). Observer-relative distinguishability is an operational relation: whether \\(O\\) can maintain the distinction between \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) above \\(I_N(O)\\). Observer-relative accessibility is consequently a relation over the Library rather than a criterion that determines which configurations belong to it."
